# Repository-wide ignores.
#
# This lives at the root, and in its own commit, on purpose. Build output is generated by
# whatever is in the tree at the time, so an ignore file that ships inside a feature directory
# disappears when that feature is reverted — leaving the artefacts it was ignoring suddenly
# visible to git, and a `git add -A` after a rollback then commits a few hundred build files.
#
# Keeping the rules here and isolating them in one commit means a rollback can revert the
# feature and keep the ignores: revert the range and exclude this commit.

# .NET build output
bin/
obj/
artifacts/
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/

# Test and coverage output
TestResults/
*.trx
*.coverage
coverage*.json
coverage*.xml
coverage*.info

# IDE
.vs/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo

# NuGet
*.nupkg
packages/

# OS
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
